    "narrative": "Our lineup for August 24th is anchored by two high-upside outfielders facing favorable conditions. **Corbin Carroll** leads the pack with a 74.65 score; while he faces a respectable arm in Kevin Gausman, his elite sprint speed against a pitcher with a slower delivery makes him a prime candidate for a stolen base, driving his projection well above the base rate. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** (72.23) is a strong start against Merrill Kelly. Kelly\u2019s high xERA (5.27) provides a massive ceiling for **Seiya Suzuki**, and being slotted in the #2 hole ensures maximum plate appearance volume. **Max Muncy** (61.65) also clears the 60-point threshold, benefiting from a friendly park factor and the opportunity to exploit a matchup against Zebby Matthews, where his power profile remains our best bet for counting stats outside of the primary outfield tier.\n\nThe decision to bench **Griffin Conine** (35.12) was the most difficult call of the day. Despite an encouraging xwOBA of .383, the combination of a difficult matchup against Ranger Suarez and a lowly #8 spot in the lineup depressed his efficiency score below the utility threshold. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Josh Naylor** (46.99) and **Zach McKinstry** (41.67); both are facing elite pitchers in Zack Wheeler and Drew Rasmussen, respectively. While **Zach McKinstry** gets a marginal boost from projected wind conditions, both players are effectively serving as \"floor\" plays today. Note that all lineup slots remain subject to change, as official cards are currently pending; we have assumed standard placement for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Travis Bazzana**, and **Mickey Moniak**, but any major shifts in the #1 through #4 spots could necessitate a re-evaluation of our daily cap usage.",
